# Turns the `engines` field in package.json from a warning into a refusal.
#
# This exists because of a real failure: the lockfiles were written by npm 11 while CI ran
# Node 22 (npm 10), which resolves optional platform dependencies differently. `npm ci` on
# the runner refused the tree with "Missing: @emnapi/runtime from lock file" and the build
# broke on main. A warning would not have stopped that; nothing reads warnings.
#
# Scope note: this only gates *this* project's own `engines`. Verified that no dependency
# in the tree declares a range that trips it, so it fails for one reason only — the local
# Node or npm major does not match `.nvmrc` and CI.
#
# Never put a registry token in this file. `.gitignore` ignores `.npmrc` everywhere for
# exactly that reason and negates only this one, at the repository root.
engine-strict=true
